@startuml activity-emails
' Spec 004 — emails to the employer and to Admins (REQ-004-9, -10)
title Emails (REQ-004-9/10)

start
if (What happened?) then (an employer submitted\nor resubmitted a listing (003))
  :The submission is saved first;
  note left
    A withdrawal sends nothing.
  end note
  :For every Admin except the person
  who submitted: send "A listing is
  waiting for approval" with the title,
  business, region and a link to its Admin view;
  if (Email could be sent?) then (no)
    :The submission still stands. The employer
    sees nothing unusual. The listing is in the
    queue and counted on the Admin area;
  else (yes)
  endif
  stop
else (an Admin approved, rejected,\ntook down or edited a listing)
  :The decision is saved first;
  if (The Admin owns the listing?) then (yes)
    :No email — nobody is emailed
    about their own action;
    stop
  else (no)
  endif
  switch (Decision)
  case (approved)
    :"Your listing is published";
  case (rejected)
    :"Your listing needs changes"
    with the reason, and that it can
    be edited and sent again;
  case (taken down)
    :"Your listing was taken down"
    with the reason;
  case (edited)
    :"We edited your listing"
    with the names of the parts changed
    (short names such as "Area",
    no old or new text);
  endswitch
  :Send one email to the owner's account address from
  hello@jairojobs.com, with the title, what the employer can
  do next, and a link to the listing in My listings;
  note right
    Sent whatever the owner's role is now. An owner
    who can no longer open My listings (an Admin
    demoted to Candidate) is refused by the link.
    Not handled here — handed to spec 008.
  end note
  if (Email could be sent?) then (no)
    :The decision still stands. Tell the Admin
    the employer could not be emailed.
    No second attempt. The employer still
    sees the outcome in My listings;
  else (yes)
  endif
  stop
endif
@enduml
